---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';

const updated = '18 September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Coravant Limited collects, uses and protects personal data through this website."
>
  <section class="shell max-w-3xl py-16 sm:py-20">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <div class="copy mt-10">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.legalName}, registered in England and Wales under company number {site.companyNumber},
        at {site.address.street}, {site.address.locality}, {site.address.postcode}. We are the data
        controller for personal data collected through this website. You can reach us at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>When you contact us.</strong> Our enquiry and booking forms are provided by Tally,
        and collect your name, email address, company and whatever you choose to tell us about your
        enquiry. We use this only to respond to you and, if we go on to work together, to manage
        that relationship. Our lawful basis is legitimate interests, specifically responding to
        people who ask us to get in touch. Those forms are protected from automated abuse by Google
        reCAPTCHA, which means Google receives your IP address and some information about your
        browser when a form is displayed. Google's privacy notice applies to that processing.
      </p>
      {
        site.analytics.cloudflareToken && (
          <p>
            <strong>When you browse.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts visits
            without cookies and without collecting anything that identifies you personally. It runs
            for every visitor because it does not process personal data in a way that requires
            consent.
          </p>
        )
      }
      <p>
        <strong>If you accept cookies.</strong> We use Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages
        are useful. It sets cookies and is loaded only after you accept. If you decline, or ignore
        the banner, it is never loaded. You can change your mind by clearing this site's data in
        your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Who your data is shared with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data and we do not share it for marketing. Data is processed on our
        behalf by Tally (form submissions), Cloudflare (website hosting{site.analytics.cloudflareToken ? ' and analytics' : ''}),
        Google (form spam protection, and analytics where you have consented)
        {site.cal.link ? ', Cal.com (appointment booking, where you use it)' : ''} and our email
        provider. Each is bound by a data processing agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries that do not become work are deleted after two years. Where we go on to work
        together, we keep records for six years after the end of the engagement to meet our legal
        and accounting obligations. Analytics data is retained for fourteen months.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about you, to have it
        corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict how we use it, and to receive it in a
        portable format. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond
        within one month.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the Information
        Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a> or on
        0303 123 1113.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies unless you accept them. If you do, Google Analytics sets cookies
        that measure page views and how visitors move through the site. Your theme preference and
        your cookie choice are stored in your browser's local storage, which never leaves your
        device and is not used to track you.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change how we handle personal data we will update this page and the date at the top
        of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
